WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.699
Friday afternoon.

00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:04.458
Morgan runs a small community learning program.

00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:10.075
For this course, we’ll follow Harbor Learning
Circle, an illustrative case built from
fictional records.

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:13.633
Someone suggests adding a free digital-skills
session next month.

00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:20.272
Three notes are on the table: an attendance
count, a facilitator availability note, and a
room-capacity note.

00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:31.252
An assistant can turn those into a neat
recommendation in seconds.

00:00:38.135 --> 00:00:40.769
But if Morgan asks, ‘Where did this come from?’

00:00:47.652 --> 00:00:50.044
a polished paragraph is thin protection.

00:00:56.927 --> 00:00:58.117
The work needs a trail.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.595
Our job today is small: design one preparation
role and one receipt.

00:01:13.612 --> 00:01:16.553
The agent does not decide whether the session
happens.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:23.527
It prepares a Session Option Brief for Morgan
to review.

00:01:27.544 --> 00:01:29.160
That distinction matters.

00:01:33.178 --> 00:01:38.853
If we give the system a loose command like ‘run
the workshop program,’ we have no useful
boundary.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:44.882
What exactly begins its work?

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:50.111
What can it read?

00:01:54.128 --> 00:01:55.770
What must it hand back?

00:01:59.787 --> 00:02:01.270
Who owns the outcome?

00:02:05.287 --> 00:02:07.865
These are ordinary management questions.

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:15.983
They become more urgent when a tool can produce
work while nobody is watching.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:29.597
Write the job in one sentence: ‘When Morgan
requests a monthly session review, prepare one
brief comparing a proposed free session against
the three cleared inputs.’

00:02:35.374 --> 00:02:37.641
The trigger is Morgan's request.

00:02:43.418 --> 00:02:45.642
The output is a draft brief.

00:02:51.419 --> 00:02:52.313
The manager is Morgan.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:05.869
The measure is whether Morgan can check the
claim and source for every recommendation
without chasing the agent through a log.

00:03:11.646 --> 00:03:18.074
The forbidden actions are just as plain: no
booking, no announcement, no message to
participants, no spending.

00:03:23.851 --> 00:03:29.223
A useful agent job names the work it finishes
and the work it leaves alone.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.906
Now attach the receipt.

00:03:43.257 --> 00:03:46.397
Imagine the brief says the room can hold twenty
people.

00:03:52.748 --> 00:04:01.202
Morgan needs to see which note supplied that
number, when the brief was prepared, what the
agent actually did, and whether anyone approved
it.

00:04:07.553 --> 00:04:13.271
The receipt also records cost or resource use,
outcome, and how to pull the draft back.

00:04:19.622 --> 00:04:21.531
A blank field stays blank and gets an owner.

00:04:27.882 --> 00:04:31.696
We never fill a gap with a confident guess.

00:04:38.047 --> 00:04:43.649
The first receipt is a handoff a busy person
can understand; the engineering log can remain
behind it.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.255
In our case, approval is ‘pending Morgan.’

00:04:57.795 --> 00:05:00.189
The outcome is ‘draft prepared, no session
selected.’

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:11.568
The rollback is ‘withdraw the draft from the
review folder and mark it superseded.’

00:05:16.109 --> 00:05:20.101
If the source for room capacity is missing,
mark the brief blocked.

00:05:24.641 --> 00:05:31.454
A complete-looking card without a source can
move bad information faster than an obviously
unfinished one.

00:05:35.995 --> 00:05:40.460
The receipt makes that gap visible before
anyone treats the draft as a decision.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.017
Take a moment.

00:05:46.826 --> 00:05:49.353
Picture one workflow in your own work.

00:05:50.162 --> 00:05:53.297
Keep this exercise on paper or in a local
draft.

00:05:54.106 --> 00:05:56.619
Use a fictional or approved example.

00:05:57.428 --> 00:05:59.976
Do not use private operational data.

00:06:00.785 --> 00:06:04.191
What is the one useful output, and who would
have to defend it?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.478
Fill the Job and Receipt boxes.

00:06:07.728 --> 00:06:12.380
Name the trigger, permitted inputs, output,
human manager, success check, and three
forbidden actions.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:15.859
Then fill the nine receipt fields for one
imaginary run.

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:24.064
If you cannot name a source, approval state, or
rollback, write ‘unknown’ and the person who
must resolve it.

00:06:24.314 --> 00:06:27.240
Do not open a real system to complete this
exercise.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:34.545
The point is to see the shape of the work
before asking a tool to do it.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.925
Save those two boxes in your Agentified
Operating File as a draft.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:36.945
Your stop condition is simple: if the owner,
source, or review gate is missing, the draft
stays on paper.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:41.586
Next we will name the decision Morgan actually
owns.
